    "text":  "National University of Computer \u0026 Emerging Sciences - NUCES - Karachi Department of Artificial Intelligence BOUNDARY DETECTION (EDGE DETECTION) it E, Input: Original Scene (Intensity \u0026 Color) Output: Edge Map (Significant Changes in Intensity) Isolating structural information to simplify image interpretation and feature extraction. 3.1 Sobel Edge Detection Sobel edge detection is a basic gradient-based method. It applies convolution with two 3x3 kernels to calculate the gradient in the horizontal and vertical directions. The magnitude of the gradient represents the strength of the edge, and its direction indicates the edge\u0027s orientation. SOBEL EDGE DETECTION OPERATOR INPUT FAST NUCES - CONVOLUTION KERNELS G = GX2 + Gy2 GRADIENT COMPONENTS Karachi Gy Output Highlighting horizontal edges Talha Shahid FINAL MAGNITUDE Final Edge Magnitude (G) 6",
